# What Docker must NOT ship as build context.
#
# Without this file the entire working directory is packed up and sent to the
# builder on every deploy. On the production VPS that was 16.79 GB, which took
# ~30 minutes to transfer before any build step ran, and was then copied twice
# more by Nixpacks (COPY . /app) for another ~20 minutes. The actual work -
# `npm install` - takes about 90 seconds.
#
# Everything listed here is either reinstalled during the build, regenerated,
# or has no business inside a container image.

# Reinstalled by `npm install` in the image. Shipping the host's copy is both
# slow and wrong: native modules built for the host may not match the image.
node_modules
Frontend/node_modules

# Full repository history. Never read at runtime.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Backups and archives. `code_23May.zip` alone is 6.28 GB.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bak
*.dump

# Database dumps. migration/*.sql is kept - it is small and applied on start.
*.sql
!migration/*.sql
migration/database/

# Frontend build output. The SERVED bundle is the repo-root `dist/`, which is
# committed. Frontend/dist is only the intermediate build directory.
Frontend/dist

# Logs and caches
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.npm
.eslintcache

# Local environment files. Real values come from Easypanel's Environment tab;
# copying a stray .env into the image would silently override them.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
Frontend/.env
Frontend/.env.*

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: .nixpacks must NOT be ignored. Nixpacks generates the Dockerfile inside
# it and that Dockerfile does
#   COPY .nixpacks/nixpkgs-<hash>.nix .nixpacks/nixpkgs-<hash>.nix
# so excluding the directory makes the build fail at that step with
# "failed to compute cache key: /.nixpacks/nixpkgs-<hash>.nix: not found".

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind-mounted directories
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both of these are BIND MOUNTS in Easypanel (Mounts tab):
#
#   /etc/easypanel/projects/digibizz_program/lms/...  ->  /app/uploads
#   /etc/easypanel/projects/digibizz_program/lms/...  ->  /app/certificateBGImages
#
# A bind mount shadows whatever the image holds at that path, so the container
# ALWAYS reads the host directory and never the baked-in copy. Shipping them in
# the build context is therefore pure waste - it cannot affect runtime.
#
# uploads/ is gitignored and holds every student photo, document and earning
# proof since launch; it is the bulk of the 16.79 GB context.
# certificateBGImages/ is tracked but 66 MB of PNGs, copied three times per
# build (context + two COPY layers).
#
# If either mount is ever REMOVED in Easypanel, delete the matching line here -
# otherwise uploads 404 and certificate generation loses its backgrounds.
uploads
certificateBGImages
